  "applicability_scope": [
    "Level 1 review of the public and canonical P01 Theorem 7.1 string statements and their statement-relevant definitions, reported by Peng Zhang.",
    "A countably indexed family of infinite languages of finite words, supplied List A equivalence to Nat, and uniform membership-oracle interface; the hidden target index is not a generator input.",
    "Exact positive presentations may repeat observations. Each supplied prompt is robust in every candidate language: for every candidate and every length bound there exists a sufficiently long continuation, which may depend on both.",
    "For every sequence of robust prompts, eventually every output extends the current prompt, belongs to the presented target, and is outside the observed sample. Generated outputs are not required to be pairwise distinct.",
    "Recursive project-local definition bodies and supporting proof-certificate types guard the meaning of the concrete-output statement only; this dependency tracking does not extend the human audit to construction or proof correspondence."
  ],
